Part 2: gold_regime_aggregator.py (Process 3 — Gold Breadth, GEX, Max Pain & IVR)

This module queries your Silver tables via QuackEngine (DuckDB 2.0) using .sql(...).pl(), computes Net Dealer Gamma Exposure (GEX), Max Pain strike, ATM IV & IV Rank (IVR), Put-Call Ratio (PCR), and NIFTY 500 Market Breadth, and outputs the unified Gold Regime artifact ready for both Parquet persistence and live Redis publishing.

Mathematical Conventions Used

• Dealer GEX (Standard Market-Maker Convention): Dealers are assumed net long Calls (+Gamma) and net short Puts (-Gamma):
\(\text{GEX}_{\text{strike}}=\left(\text{OI}_{\text{CE}}\cdot \Gamma _{\text{CE}}-\text{OI}_{\text{PE}}\cdot \Gamma _{\text{PE}}\right)\times \text{LotSize}\times \text{Spot}^{2}\times 0.01\)
(Positive Net GEX = volatility dampening / dealer mean-reversion hedging; Negative Net GEX = volatility amplifying / trend acceleration).
• Max Pain: The candidate expiry strike \(K^{*}\) that minimizes total intrinsic payout across all open Call and Put contracts:
\(K^{*}=\arg \min _{K}\sum _{i}\left[\text{OI}_{\text{CE},i}\cdot \max (0,K-K_{i})+\text{OI}_{\text{PE},i}\cdot \max (0,K_{i}-K)\right]\)
